From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Commit pointer constraint updates independently of
 client presentation.

The child-presentation changes in 6bc30234 stopped committing an unchanged
parent after every client present. WAYLAND_ClipCursor still relies on those
incidental commits: it commits the cursor position hint before replacing a
pointer lock, then only flushes the connection after updating the constraint.

Confinement region updates are double-buffered. KWin also buffers constraint
creation and destruction on the constrained surface. Without a subsequent
parent commit, a restored visible cursor can remain locked in the compositor
while Wine has already destroyed its locked-pointer proxy. Relative motion
continues, but absolute motion and the visible cursor only recover when a
focus or window-state change commits the parent again. The 11-6/11-7 logs in
issue #794 show this sequence in both Slay the Spire 2 and Tomb Raider.

Commit the constrained surface after updating the constraint, then flush.
Keep the pre-unlock hint commit, since the position hint must take effect
before destroying the lock. Acquire the window-data lock only after dropping
the pointer lock, and check the surface identity before committing it.

This does not restore per-frame parent commits, change cursor visibility
semantics, or depend on the Steam overlay.

Issue: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/794
Protocol: https://wayland.app/protocols/pointer-constraints-unstable-v1
KWin: https://invent.kde.org/plasma/kwin/-/blob/master/src/wayland/pointerconstraints_v1.cpp
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
@@ -1252,6 +1252,16 @@ BOOL WAYLAND_ClipCursor(const RECT *clip, BOOL reset)
                                       FALSE);
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&pointer->mutex);
 
+    /* Constraint state belongs to the parent surface, not the independently
+     * presented client. Flush alone does not apply double-buffered state.
+     * Keep the earlier hint commit before unlocking the pointer as well. */
+    if (wl_surface && (data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd)))
+    {
+        if (data->wayland_surface && data->wayland_surface->wl_surface == wl_surface)
+            wl_surface_commit(wl_surface);
+        wayland_win_data_release(data);
+    }
+
     wl_display_flush(process_wayland.wl_display);
 
     return TRUE;
